    "body": "### Problem\n\n### Problem Description\n\nWith ui2 enabled, when `laststatus=0` is set (with `ruler=true` or `showtabline`), saving a modified buffer via `:w` successfully writes the file and resets `&modified` to `0`, but the UI fails to trigger an immediate redraw sweep. As a result, the `[+]` modified indicator remains visible on screen after `:w` completes.\n\nThe `[+]` indicator only disappears when a subsequent user input event (such as pressing `j`/`k`, moving the cursor, or running a command) forces Neovim's UI loop to process a redraw cycle. \n\nThis indicates that `BufWritePost` / write completion events are not scheduling an automatic UI/ruler/tabline redraw flush when global statuslines are disabled (`laststatus=0`).\n\n### Minimal Reproduction Script (`repro.lua`)\n\n```lua\n-- repro.lua\n-- Run with: nvim --clean -u repro.lua test.txt\n\nrequire('vim._core.ui2').enable({\n  enable = true, -- Whether to enable or disable the UI.\n  msg = { -- Options related to the message module.\n    ---@type 'cmd'|'msg' Default message target, either in the\n    ---cmdline or in a separate ephemeral message window.\n    ---@type string|table<string, 'cmd'|'msg'|'pager'> Default message target\n    ---or table mapping |ui-messages| kinds and triggers to a target.\n    targets = 'cmd',\n    cmd = { -- Options related to messages in the cmdline window.\n      height = 0.5 -- Maximum height while expanded for messages beyond 'cmdheight'.\n    },\n    dialog = { -- Options related to dialog window.\n      height = 0.5, -- Maximum height.\n    },\n    msg = { -- Options related to msg window.\n      height = 0.5, -- Maximum height.\n      timeout = 4000, -- Time a message is visible in the message window.\n    },\n    pager = { -- Options related to message window.\n      height = 1, -- Maximum height.\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n\nvim.opt.laststatus = 0\nvim.opt.rulerformat = \"%60(%=%m %t %l:%c%)\"\nvim.opt.ruler = true\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Launch Neovim with the clean reproduction script:\n   ```bash\n   nvim --clean -u repro.lua test.txt\n   ```\n2. Make an edit in insert mode (e.g., type `ihello<Esc>`). Notice the `[+]` indicator appears in the ruler/tabline.\n3. Save the file:\n   ```vim\n   :w\n   ```\n4. **Observe:** The file writes successfully, but the `[+]` indicator remains visible in the UI.\n5. Press any movement key (e.g., `j` or `k`).\n6. **Observe:** The `[+]` indicator immediately disappears.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSaving the file via `:w` should automatically flush a UI/ruler/tabline redraw sweep regardless of `laststatus` settings, clearing the `[+]` modified indicator immediately upon write.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.5\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, ui2 is a nvim-only feature\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.49.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nArch system package manager (pacman) /extra/neovim",
